WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.240
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.510 --> 01:34.870
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.390 --> 01:37.700
[Episode 6]

4
01:38.460 --> 01:40.259
Hurry up. They'll be hungry soon.

5
01:39.490 --> 01:43.330
[Rucheng, Hunan; The Red Army's Temporary Encampment]

6
01:40.560 --> 01:41.039
Okay.

7
01:48.870 --> 01:49.759
Slow down.

8
01:50.330 --> 01:51.050
Guo.

9
01:51.780 --> 01:52.620
Guo!

10
01:53.000 --> 01:53.940
What's for lunch today?

11
01:53.940 --> 01:54.930
We're... we're going to have steamed cornbread.

12
01:54.930 --> 01:56.960
Hurry up. I'm so starving that my stomach hurts.

13
01:56.960 --> 01:57.810
Okay, okay.

14
02:03.480 --> 02:04.510
Here. Okay.

15
02:07.120 --> 02:08.000
Make it good.

16
02:08.620 --> 02:10.310
Guo, why did you take my flute?

17
02:11.860 --> 02:12.860
Give it back to me.

18
02:13.220 --> 02:14.090
Just borrowing it.

19
02:14.090 --> 02:15.150
Guo, this is a flute.

20
02:15.150 --> 02:16.550
Not a blowpipe.

21
02:16.910 --> 02:18.360
Well, it's a tube too.

22
02:18.360 --> 02:19.520
Tell me, you're a cook.

23
02:19.520 --> 02:22.000
Why do you always keep a tube at your waist?

24
02:22.390 --> 02:23.000
Hurry up and let me use it.

25
02:23.000 --> 02:24.490
My dad left this for me.

26
02:26.520 --> 02:28.240
My dad died in Guangchang.

27
02:28.860 --> 02:30.190
He left nothing behind.

28
02:30.920 --> 02:32.890
He only left me this flute.

29
02:47.650 --> 02:48.310
Which room?

30
02:48.310 --> 02:49.440
I'll move it for you.

31
02:50.579 --> 02:52.780
Chairman, it's just around the corner.

32
02:55.910 --> 02:57.030
Be careful.

33
02:58.300 --> 02:58.970
Thank you.

34
02:59.000 --> 02:59.730
It's okay. Just put it here.

35
02:59.730 --> 03:00.860
I'll move it myself.

36
03:02.170 --> 03:03.100
This is the room.

37
03:12.080 --> 03:13.840
Comrades, who let you stay here?

38
03:13.840 --> 03:15.440
We claimed this house first.

39
03:15.470 --> 03:16.630
What's this about yours and ours?

40
03:16.630 --> 03:17.150
Make way. Make way.

41
03:17.150 --> 03:18.470
Our stay here was arranged by the regiment.

42
03:18.300 --> 03:19.370
[Mao Zedong, Chairman of the Central Executive Committee]

43
03:18.890 --> 03:20.590
If you have any problems, go talk to our regiment commander.

44
03:19.370 --> 03:20.450
[of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

45
03:20.610 --> 03:21.540
You think you're right?

46
03:21.540 --> 03:23.000
We clearly claimed this house first.

47
03:23.000 --> 03:24.240
Do you know who this is for?

48
03:24.240 --> 03:25.300
Make way. Make way.

49
03:25.860 --> 03:26.440
Don't block the way.

50
03:26.440 --> 03:27.000
Careful.

51
03:27.030 --> 03:28.880
Do you know who this is for?

52
03:28.920 --> 03:30.720
Chen, there are too many people.

53
03:31.450 --> 03:32.880
There aren't enough houses.

54
03:32.880 --> 03:33.590
Let's go.

55
03:33.610 --> 03:34.600
I'll go find their regiment commander.

56
03:34.600 --> 03:35.600
Hu.

57
03:36.780 --> 03:37.470
By going to their regimental commander...

58
03:37.470 --> 03:38.400
Make way, make way.

59
03:38.400 --> 03:39.160
Come on. Make way.

60
03:39.160 --> 03:39.710
Be careful.

61
03:39.710 --> 03:40.400
Be careful.

62
03:40.570 --> 03:41.540
Squad leader.

63
03:41.570 --> 03:43.870
Can this plank from a local be used as a bed?

64
03:43.870 --> 03:44.730
Who are you trying to get kicked out of here

65
03:44.730 --> 03:46.990
by going to their regimental commander?

66
03:47.150 --> 03:48.100
Make way, comrade.

67
03:48.100 --> 03:48.970
Make way, make way.

68
03:48.970 --> 03:49.740
Be careful.

69
03:52.430 --> 03:54.090
Chairman, you're still sick.

70
03:54.400 --> 03:55.730
You can't stay outside.

71
03:55.970 --> 03:58.100
Didn't your guard squad claim a house?

72
03:58.120 --> 04:00.080
I'll just make do with you for one night.

73
04:00.080 --> 04:01.850
Chairman, ours is not a house.

74
04:02.080 --> 04:03.480
It's just a broken shack.

75
04:03.580 --> 04:04.870
It's drafty and very cold.

76
04:04.870 --> 04:06.930
We'll squeeze in. It'll keep us warm.

77
04:07.950 --> 04:08.580
Hurry up.

78
04:10.760 --> 04:11.690
I'll move this.

79
04:11.760 --> 04:12.570
Come on.

80
04:16.610 --> 04:17.339
Take it over.

81
04:23.150 --> 04:23.830
Put it here?

82
04:24.190 --> 04:25.080
Everything is moved.

83
04:25.080 --> 04:25.790
Okay.

84
04:28.800 --> 04:30.650
Kid, time to eat.

85
04:31.720 --> 04:32.680
Still angry?

86
04:35.920 --> 04:37.490
You have to eat even if you're angry.

87
04:37.490 --> 04:38.240
Let me tell you,

88
04:38.240 --> 04:40.720
today's cornbread is better than ever.

89
04:40.760 --> 04:42.790
It has more cornmeal and is sweet.

90
04:42.940 --> 04:43.670
Have a taste.

91
04:44.190 --> 04:45.159
Guo.

92
04:45.260 --> 04:46.230
You're wrong.

93
04:46.820 --> 04:48.840
You shouldn't have taken this kid's flute.

94
04:48.840 --> 04:49.840
I have to criticize you.

95
04:49.840 --> 04:50.900
Yes, it's my fault.

96
04:50.980 --> 04:51.850
Your criticism is right.

97
04:51.850 --> 04:53.170
It is your fault.

98
04:54.180 --> 04:55.790
I just kept seeing that

99
04:55.820 --> 04:58.060
he had a flute tucked in his waist but couldn't play it,

100
04:58.060 --> 04:58.530
so I took it...

101
04:58.530 --> 04:59.650
Who says I can't?

102
04:59.870 --> 05:01.600
You've never played it before.

103
05:21.760 --> 05:23.520
Not bad, right?

104
05:23.550 --> 05:24.750
He's got some skills.

105
05:47.430 --> 05:49.159
Great!

106
05:49.190 --> 05:49.600
Great!

107
05:49.600 --> 05:51.000
One more!

108
05:51.060 --> 05:51.900
One more!

109
05:52.190 --> 05:53.120
Great!

110
05:54.159 --> 05:57.240
One more!

111
06:04.130 --> 06:06.860
Kid, why did you follow us again?

112
06:07.080 --> 06:08.190
You must be hungry.

113
06:09.270 --> 06:10.120
Eat this.

114
06:11.320 --> 06:12.250
Go ahead and eat.

115
06:12.320 --> 06:13.440
Eat this.

116
06:14.120 --> 06:18.600
Guo, how many days has this kid been following us?

117
06:18.800 --> 06:20.630
He's been following us since Yudu.

118
06:20.630 --> 06:22.750
He used to follow the 6th Company.

119
06:23.500 --> 06:24.430
The 6th Company?

120
06:25.670 --> 06:27.200
Here, take this cornbread.

121
06:27.340 --> 06:28.560
Don't follow us anymore.

122
06:28.560 --> 06:31.420
The Red Army is going to fight. It's very dangerous.

123
06:32.810 --> 06:34.130
I'm not a beggar.

124
06:35.130 --> 06:37.409
I'm a member of the Children's Corps in Xingguo County.

125
06:37.409 --> 06:38.610
Then why are you here?

126
06:38.620 --> 06:40.080
I want to join the Red Army.

127
06:40.960 --> 06:42.620
They thought I was too young and didn't want me.

128
06:42.620 --> 06:43.950
So I just followed them.

129
06:44.070 --> 06:45.130
You are indeed too young.

130
06:45.130 --> 06:46.860
You're not even as tall as a gun.

131
06:47.200 --> 06:49.330
There are children in your ranks, too.

132
06:54.710 --> 06:57.150
I've seen ones smaller than me.

133
06:57.280 --> 06:58.610
I heard them singing.

134
06:58.920 --> 07:00.040
I can sing too.

135
07:00.190 --> 07:01.520
I sing better than them.

136
07:01.750 --> 07:03.120
Chairman Mao knows me.

137
07:03.250 --> 07:04.180
You know Chairman Mao?

138
07:04.180 --> 07:04.980
Chairman Mao?

139
07:06.360 --> 07:08.720
I know. He's talking about the propaganda troupe.

140
07:08.720 --> 07:10.370
Okay, I'll take you there.

141
07:10.550 --> 07:12.680
But I don't know if they'll accept you.

142
07:14.540 --> 07:15.600
You must be hungry.

143
07:16.490 --> 07:18.900
Here, take it and eat.

144
07:20.710 --> 07:21.290
Eat.

145
07:26.180 --> 07:27.840
Let's go. I'll take you there.

146
07:27.950 --> 07:28.970
Guo, I'll go over first.

147
07:28.970 --> 07:29.670
Okay, okay.

148
07:52.320 --> 07:54.850
Who is Mr. Luo, head of the propaganda troupe?

149
07:55.159 --> 07:56.190
I am the head.

150
07:56.480 --> 07:58.340
I am Luo Dahua. What's the matter?

151
07:58.430 --> 08:00.190
I'm the commander of the 3rd Company.

152
08:00.190 --> 08:02.390
This kid has been following us for days.

153
08:02.430 --> 08:03.750
He wants to join the Red Army.

154
08:03.750 --> 08:05.720
But we are a combat unit,

155
08:05.740 --> 08:06.750
which is not suitable for him.

156
08:06.750 --> 08:08.210
So I brought him here to ask

157
08:08.290 --> 08:09.770
if you can take him in.

158
08:09.980 --> 08:10.730
Commander,

159
08:10.760 --> 08:12.280
we are not a shelter.

160
08:12.580 --> 08:14.820
Besides, this kid is too young.

161
08:15.090 --> 08:16.210
How am I young?

162
08:16.390 --> 08:18.100
I sing better than all of you.

163
08:18.290 --> 08:19.410
You talk big.

164
08:19.770 --> 08:21.100
What songs can you sing?

165
08:21.190 --> 08:22.920
I can sing whatever you can.

166
08:23.190 --> 08:25.040
Then sing one for us to hear.

167
08:25.180 --> 08:25.660
Okay.

168
08:25.990 --> 08:27.040
Then I'll sing

169
08:27.240 --> 08:29.070
"To Be a Soldier, Join the Red Army."

170
08:29.070 --> 08:29.480
Great.

171
08:29.510 --> 08:30.120
Great.

172
08:30.120 --> 08:31.310
Sing one.

173
08:33.750 --> 08:35.940
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

174
08:36.159 --> 08:38.549
♪ Workers and peasants unite to fight the enemy ♪

175
08:38.630 --> 08:40.880
♪ Against the gentry, landlords, and Kuomingtang ♪

176
08:41.200 --> 08:43.559
♪ Show them no mercy at all ♪

177
08:43.610 --> 08:45.730
♪ To be a soldier, join the Red Army ♪

178
08:46.000 --> 08:48.030
♪ The Red and White Armies are worlds apart ♪

179
08:48.270 --> 08:50.240
♪ White Army soldiers are treated like beasts of burden ♪

180
08:50.480 --> 08:52.750
♪ Red Army officers and men are brothers ♪

181
08:52.770 --> 08:54.770
Great!

182
08:56.910 --> 08:58.460
Kid, what's your name?

183
08:59.010 --> 09:00.610
My name is Xie Xingguo.

184
09:01.840 --> 09:02.600
Commander.

185
09:02.670 --> 09:04.180
We'll take this Xie Xingguo.

186
09:04.180 --> 09:05.770
Good, that's great.

187
09:08.970 --> 09:11.920
Did you just say you're taking me?

188
09:12.370 --> 09:13.450
Comrade Xie Xingguo,

189
09:13.450 --> 09:15.680
welcome to the propaganda troupe of the 1st Red Army Corps.

190
09:15.680 --> 09:16.760
Welcome.

191
09:16.850 --> 09:18.240
Welcome.

192
09:21.570 --> 09:22.930
Did you just say

193
09:24.030 --> 09:25.360
I'm in the Red Army now?

194
09:25.760 --> 09:27.420
I'm really in the Red Army now.

195
09:28.010 --> 09:29.540
You're one of us from now on.

196
09:30.210 --> 09:33.010
Okay. Okay.

197
10:04.900 --> 10:08.820
"How can I last till dawn in this leaking, rain-soaked bed?"

198
10:17.460 --> 10:18.460
Changbao.

199
10:20.760 --> 10:22.800
This is how I feel right now.

200
10:24.250 --> 10:26.650
"How can I get tens of thousands of mansions

201
10:27.090 --> 10:30.750
to shelter all the poor scholars in the world and make them smile?"

202
11:31.890 --> 11:32.730
Changbao.

203
11:34.070 --> 11:34.880
Changbao.

204
11:36.080 --> 11:38.050
Wash your feet before you sleep.

205
11:40.260 --> 11:42.590
Why wash my feet in the middle of the night?

206
11:43.740 --> 11:45.900
Chairman, you should rest early too.

207
12:06.210 --> 12:07.040
What's wrong?

208
12:07.130 --> 12:07.930
Chairman,

209
12:08.740 --> 12:11.650
you're right. Feet do need washing.

210
12:12.530 --> 12:14.690
Good, then go wash them quickly.

211
12:15.310 --> 12:17.380
No, we both need to wash our feet.

212
12:17.780 --> 12:19.440
I'll fetch some water for you.

213
12:28.670 --> 12:29.270
Changbao.

214
12:30.190 --> 12:31.450
Bring me the map first.

215
12:31.600 --> 12:32.210
Okay.

216
13:04.650 --> 13:07.320
We have sent telegrams

217
13:07.360 --> 13:10.760
to the 2nd and 6th Army Corps twice in a row,

218
13:08.340 --> 13:10.230
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Head of the CPC Central Committee]

219
13:11.030 --> 13:14.700
disapproving of their plan to merge operations.

220
13:14.190 --> 13:15.220
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee,]

221
13:14.790 --> 13:16.360
But why do they still turn a deaf ear

222
13:15.220 --> 13:15.740
[Vice Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,]

223
13:15.740 --> 13:16.260
[and Political Commissar-General of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

224
13:16.440 --> 13:17.790
[Wu Xiuquan, Translator]

225
13:16.510 --> 13:18.230
and advance together towards northwestern Hunan?

226
13:18.030 --> 13:19.880
[Zhu De, Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

227
13:19.780 --> 13:21.000
This is a blatant defiance of the orders

228
13:19.880 --> 13:21.730
[and Commander-in-Chief of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

229
13:21.020 --> 13:22.330
of the Central Committee and the Military Commission.

230
13:22.330 --> 13:24.590
This is a serious organizational error.

231
13:25.300 --> 13:26.690
[Li De, Comintern Military Advisor]

232
13:28.790 --> 13:32.300
I don't think the situation is necessarily that serious.

233
13:32.880 --> 13:35.000
We don't understand the current situation

234
13:35.000 --> 13:36.020
of the 2nd and 6th Army Corps.

235
13:36.020 --> 13:37.140
Their joint action

236
13:37.380 --> 13:40.040
might be conducive to creating a new situation.

237
13:41.320 --> 13:42.580
Let's leave it at that.

238
13:42.640 --> 13:44.590
Let's shelve this issue for now.

239
13:45.030 --> 13:46.830
We'll see what their next step is

240
13:46.850 --> 13:48.370
before making a decision.

241
13:48.970 --> 13:50.650
I have some new information to share.

242
13:50.650 --> 13:52.720
According to the enemy telegrams deciphered by the 2nd Bureau,

243
13:52.720 --> 13:54.120
Chen Jitang's main force

244
13:54.210 --> 13:56.370
has retreated to the Dayu, Nanxiong,

245
13:56.400 --> 13:57.200
and Anyuan line

246
13:57.200 --> 13:58.530
and shifted to defense.

247
13:58.710 --> 14:01.460
He Jian's Hunan Army in central and southern Hunan

248
14:01.460 --> 14:03.330
only has a small number of local troops left.

249
14:03.330 --> 14:04.280
It will take at least 20 days

250
14:04.280 --> 14:05.760
for their main force to assemble.

251
14:05.760 --> 14:08.150
Chiang Kai-shek's direct troops ordered to pursue us

252
14:08.150 --> 14:09.620
are currently still far away in Xingguo,

253
14:09.620 --> 14:11.150
Gulonggang, and Shicheng.

254
14:11.230 --> 14:14.550
They won't be able to reach southern Hunan and northern Guangdong in the short term.

255
14:14.550 --> 14:15.550
That means

256
14:15.730 --> 14:17.260
the enemy forces ahead of us

257
14:18.270 --> 14:19.840
are very weak right now.

258
14:21.120 --> 14:24.720
I have a new plan.

259
14:29.680 --> 14:32.000
We should immediately advance along

260
14:32.260 --> 14:33.590
the Jiangxi-Guangdong

261
14:33.790 --> 14:35.170
and Hunan-Guangdong borders.

262
14:35.170 --> 14:36.880
We should immediately advance along the Jiangxi-Guangdong

263
14:36.880 --> 14:38.610
and Hunan-Guangdong borders,

264
14:39.500 --> 14:40.620
pushing through the area between Rucheng in Hunan

265
14:40.620 --> 14:42.620
and Chengkou in Guangdong,

266
14:42.650 --> 14:47.670
to break through the KMT troops' second line of defense.

267
14:47.830 --> 14:50.220
Speed is crucial in war.

268
14:50.730 --> 14:52.190
No matter how fast you are,

269
14:52.200 --> 14:55.130
can you outrun Chiang Kai-shek's planes and trucks?

270
14:55.850 --> 14:56.850
Mao?

271
14:56.920 --> 14:59.420
You can't just look at what's right in front of you.

272
14:59.420 --> 15:00.890
Comrade Zedong, please sit down.

273
15:00.890 --> 15:01.890
I won't sit.

274
15:02.670 --> 15:05.870
I'm here to make a suggestion to the Military Commission.

275
15:10.620 --> 15:12.690
What is your suggestion, Comrade Mao Zedong?

276
15:12.690 --> 15:14.620
I suggest the Military Commission

277
15:14.870 --> 15:17.110
abandon the original westward plan

278
15:17.910 --> 15:20.100
and formulate a new route of action.

279
15:25.530 --> 15:26.490
The reason?

280
15:26.850 --> 15:27.810
First,

281
15:27.840 --> 15:29.710
we are currently like beggars fighting dogs,

282
15:29.710 --> 15:30.680
fighting while retreating.

283
15:30.680 --> 15:32.650
We can't move fast or escape.

284
15:32.990 --> 15:35.320
We can't disrupt the enemy's deployment,

285
15:35.330 --> 15:37.320
and we will eventually fall into a passive position.

286
15:37.320 --> 15:39.240
Second, as the art of war says,

287
15:39.630 --> 15:43.100
"March to where the enemy does not expect, and attack where they are unprepared."

288
15:43.100 --> 15:44.300
But what are we doing?

289
15:44.440 --> 15:45.840
We've been following

290
15:45.840 --> 15:48.030
the old route of the 6th Red Army Corps.

291
15:48.050 --> 15:49.600
Chiang Kai-shek is no fool.

292
15:49.760 --> 15:51.330
He will eventually figure it out.

293
15:51.330 --> 15:52.450
If we keep going like this,

294
15:52.450 --> 15:54.710
it will only get more and more dangerous.

295
15:56.200 --> 15:58.030
Mao, then tell us,

296
15:58.250 --> 15:59.530
where should we go?

297
16:00.660 --> 16:02.130
I thought about it all night.

298
16:02.130 --> 16:04.370
We should go to a place with a mass base.

299
16:04.730 --> 16:05.610
We should...

300
16:07.820 --> 16:10.460
Before the enemy completes their deployment,

301
16:11.040 --> 16:13.080
we should abandon the original westward plan

302
16:13.080 --> 16:15.680
and cross the Zhuguang Mountains to the north.

303
16:16.230 --> 16:18.770
Go north along the Lei River to shake off the enemy.

304
16:18.770 --> 16:21.030
Rest in the Shuikoushan area for a while,

305
16:21.190 --> 16:22.240
and then we will go to

306
16:22.240 --> 16:25.680
Yongfeng, Lantian, Baoqing and other places to set up a battlefield.

307
16:25.680 --> 16:26.890
Look for opportunities to annihilate the enemy.

308
16:26.890 --> 16:28.430
After breaking the enemy's deployment,

309
16:28.430 --> 16:31.200
we will make a new battle plan.

310
16:36.000 --> 16:37.170
If possible,

311
16:38.090 --> 16:39.990
we can follow the route we took to establish bases

312
16:39.990 --> 16:43.000
in southern Jiangxi and western Fujian after leaving Jinggangshan,

313
16:43.000 --> 16:47.430
and fight our way back to the Central Soviet Area.

314
16:49.080 --> 16:49.660
Mao,

315
16:49.870 --> 16:52.740
I don't know what you are thinking.

316
16:52.800 --> 16:54.330
Do you think the people here

317
16:54.590 --> 16:56.740
have no strategic mind?

318
16:56.900 --> 16:58.090
Are you trying to prove

319
16:58.090 --> 16:59.820
that we have no strategic mind?

320
17:00.630 --> 17:01.790
I'm just putting forward my views.

321
17:01.790 --> 17:03.350
I have no intention of competing with you.

322
17:03.350 --> 17:06.390
This is just my idea. I don't want to argue.

323
17:07.880 --> 17:12.220
But your idea is too strange.

324
17:12.240 --> 17:14.319
Do you think I would give up such a good opportunity

325
17:14.319 --> 17:16.750
to break through the enemy's blockade,

326
17:16.770 --> 17:22.200
and go over the mountains to run in circles with the enemy?

327
17:22.329 --> 17:24.030
Do you think I would give up such a good opportunity

328
17:24.030 --> 17:25.480
to break through the enemy's blockade,

329
17:25.480 --> 17:28.680
and go over the mountains to run in circles with the enemy?

330
17:32.680 --> 17:33.400
Mao,

331
17:33.680 --> 17:39.880
stop putting so much faith in your guerrilla tactics.

332
17:39.980 --> 17:41.220
You have no ability,

333
17:41.240 --> 17:45.610
nor the right to talk to us.

334
17:49.490 --> 17:50.640
You have no ability,

335
17:50.670 --> 17:52.840
nor the right to talk to us.

336
17:58.070 --> 17:59.090
Comrade Mao Zedong.

337
17:59.090 --> 18:00.640
We understand your idea.

338
18:01.030 --> 18:02.320
The strategic policy of the Red Army

339
18:02.320 --> 18:03.920
was decided by our "Troika",

340
18:04.080 --> 18:05.810
and approved by the Comintern.

341
18:05.830 --> 18:08.240
Besides, we just set off.

342
18:08.450 --> 18:10.250
Do you want us to turn back?

343
18:33.010 --> 18:34.600
Comrades,

344
18:35.240 --> 18:38.240
what do you think of my plan?

345
18:43.600 --> 18:44.460
Say that again.

346
18:44.790 --> 18:46.110
I plan to...

347
18:46.470 --> 18:47.390
Enlai.

348
18:48.300 --> 18:51.810
I recommend advancing along the Jiangxi-Guangdong and Hunan-Guangdong...

349
18:51.810 --> 18:55.340
I recommend advancing along the Jiangxi-Guangdong border...

350
19:03.770 --> 19:04.580
Mao.

351
19:06.460 --> 19:07.210
Mao.

352
19:08.810 --> 19:09.810
Are you okay?

353
19:11.670 --> 19:12.300
I'm fine.

354
19:14.160 --> 19:16.010
I heard there's an old doctor in town

355
19:16.010 --> 19:17.960
who specializes in treating malaria.

356
19:17.960 --> 19:19.660
I specifically asked him to prescribe some medicine.

357
19:19.660 --> 19:20.880
Take it back and boil it.

358
19:20.880 --> 19:22.260
Drink it once in the morning and once in the evening,

359
19:22.260 --> 19:23.190
after meals.

360
19:27.000 --> 19:28.590
I've got it. Let's go.

361
19:30.170 --> 19:30.960
Careful.

362
19:33.740 --> 19:35.370
One, two, up.

363
19:39.460 --> 19:40.440
Push forward. Go.

364
19:40.440 --> 19:41.280
Come on.

365
19:42.250 --> 19:43.250
Come on, make way.

366
19:47.530 --> 19:48.700
Old friend.

367
19:49.300 --> 19:50.630
The cart may be crooked,

368
19:50.950 --> 19:52.380
but as long as our men are here,

369
19:52.380 --> 19:53.550
we can set it right.

370
19:53.840 --> 19:55.100
Commander-in-Chief.

371
19:55.830 --> 19:57.560
A crooked cart can be set right.

372
19:58.370 --> 19:59.560
If we take the wrong path,

373
19:59.560 --> 20:00.620
we have to turn back

374
20:00.810 --> 20:02.070
and take many detours.

375
20:02.320 --> 20:04.910
Besides, once we take some wrong paths,

376
20:05.940 --> 20:09.230
there is simply no turning back.

377
20:38.990 --> 20:40.080
Get up.

378
20:42.000 --> 20:42.770
Fall in!

379
20:43.300 --> 20:43.920
Go, go, go.

380
20:45.270 --> 20:45.960
Hurry up!

381
20:47.400 --> 20:48.480
Wake up. Fall in.

382
20:48.880 --> 20:50.590
Get everything. Hurry up.

383
20:53.750 --> 20:55.210
Did you bring everything?

384
20:55.240 --> 20:56.110
Yes.

385
20:56.750 --> 20:58.410
-I'll go first. -I'll follow.

386
21:05.350 --> 21:08.510
Attention, everyone! Dress right, dress!

387
21:09.210 --> 21:10.020
Ready, front!

388
21:12.920 --> 21:14.890
Attention, everyone!

389
21:16.350 --> 21:17.030
Hurry up!

390
21:18.350 --> 21:19.590
Right face!

391
21:28.360 --> 21:30.010
Everyone, fall in!

392
21:32.820 --> 21:33.650
Girls.

393
21:34.270 --> 21:35.640
Are you leaving?

394
21:36.360 --> 21:37.990
Ma'am, we are setting off.

395
21:40.310 --> 21:42.440
I was wondering why I slept so soundly.

396
21:42.680 --> 21:45.290
How could you put the whole quilt on me?

397
21:48.600 --> 21:50.260
You shouldn't have done that.

398
21:50.580 --> 21:51.860
Ma'am, we are young.

399
21:51.890 --> 21:53.490
We are not afraid of the cold.

400
21:53.560 --> 21:55.120
Look, it's all my fault.

401
21:56.030 --> 21:57.160
It's cold here.

402
21:57.490 --> 21:58.340
And my family

403
21:58.420 --> 22:00.480
really has nothing to cover you with.

404
22:00.720 --> 22:02.850
You still thought of me. Seriously...

405
22:17.740 --> 22:18.930
Here, Ma'am.

406
22:19.180 --> 22:20.640
Cover the child with this.

407
22:21.340 --> 22:22.100
No, I can't.

408
22:22.210 --> 22:22.920
Just keep it.

409
22:22.920 --> 22:23.510
No, no.

410
22:23.770 --> 22:25.090
Take your quilt back.

411
22:25.550 --> 22:26.090
I can't take it.

412
22:26.090 --> 22:26.510
Take it back.

413
22:26.510 --> 22:26.980
Please keep it.

414
22:26.980 --> 22:27.490
No.

415
22:27.890 --> 22:29.810
Ma'am, our army still has more.

416
22:30.350 --> 22:32.290
The three of you only have one quilt.

417
22:32.290 --> 22:33.400
You can't fool me.

418
22:33.550 --> 22:34.880
I can't take this quilt.

419
22:34.900 --> 22:35.550
Ma'am, keep it.

420
22:35.550 --> 22:36.440
I can't take it.

421
22:36.590 --> 22:37.880
Our army really has more.

422
22:37.880 --> 22:38.590
No, no.

423
22:38.590 --> 22:39.350
I really can't.

424
22:39.350 --> 22:39.920
Keep it.

425
22:40.180 --> 22:41.780
I don't want it. Take it back.

426
22:49.470 --> 22:50.230
Scissors.

427
23:33.210 --> 23:35.300
Why are you cutting a perfectly good quilt?

428
23:35.300 --> 23:36.330
Don't cut it.

429
23:39.240 --> 23:41.520
Ma'am, sew the edges.

430
23:41.660 --> 23:43.900
Then you can make a small quilt for the child

431
23:43.900 --> 23:45.030
so he won't get cold.

432
23:47.440 --> 23:48.700
We're leaving, ma'am.

433
23:48.780 --> 23:49.870
Ma'am, we're leaving.

434
23:49.870 --> 23:51.510
Ma'am, we're leaving.

435
23:56.050 --> 23:57.010
Girls.

436
23:58.750 --> 24:00.230
When will you come back?

437
24:00.460 --> 24:03.560
Ma'am, we'll come back when the revolution is victorious.

438
24:03.560 --> 24:05.480
Ma'am, we'll come back then

439
24:05.820 --> 24:07.650
and bring you a brand-new quilt.

440
24:09.320 --> 24:11.590
Okay, you must come back.

441
24:32.580 --> 24:35.380
From November 5 to 8, 1934,

442
24:36.050 --> 24:38.280
the Central Red Army used part of its forces

443
24:38.280 --> 24:39.920
to monitor the enemy in Rucheng.

444
24:39.920 --> 24:42.840
The rest of the troops passed between Rucheng and Chengkou,

445
24:42.840 --> 24:45.720
breaking through the KMT troops' second blockade line,

446
24:45.720 --> 24:48.050
entering southern Hunan and northern Guangdong,

447
24:48.050 --> 24:50.580
and continuing towards Yizhang and Lechang.

448
24:51.530 --> 24:52.590
In early November,

449
24:52.840 --> 24:55.640
the 7th Red Army Corps broke through the enemy's heavy blockades

450
24:55.640 --> 24:58.270
and entered the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Soviet Area.

451
24:58.270 --> 25:00.590
In places like Chongxi, north of Geyuan,

452
25:00.590 --> 25:04.070
they joined forces with the 10th Red Army led by Fang Zhimin.

453
25:14.970 --> 25:17.020
[Xun Huaizhou, Commander of the 7th Red Army Corps]

454
25:17.040 --> 25:18.900
[Su Yu, Chief of Staff of the 7th Red Army Corps]

455
25:36.280 --> 25:37.910
[Fang Zhimin, Secretary of the CPC Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Provincial Committee]

456
25:37.380 --> 25:38.270
I am Fang Zhimin.

457
25:37.910 --> 25:39.550
[and Chairman of the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Provincial Soviet Government]

458
25:38.680 --> 25:39.810
I received instructions from the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

459
25:39.810 --> 25:40.940
and came to find you.

460
25:42.340 --> 25:43.470
Comrade Fang Zhimin.

461
25:43.470 --> 25:44.710
Finally we meet.

462
25:44.940 --> 25:47.920
[Zeng Hongyi, Central Representative with the 7th Red Army Corps]

463
25:45.060 --> 25:48.720
I'm Zeng Hongyi, Central Representative with the 7th Red Army Corps.

464
25:48.720 --> 25:49.720
Hello.

465
25:50.430 --> 25:52.600
This is the Political Commissar of the 7th Red Army Corps,

466
25:52.600 --> 25:53.880
Comrade Yue Shaohua.

467
25:53.740 --> 25:55.490
[Yue Shaohua, Political Commissar of the 7th Red Army Corps]

468
25:54.030 --> 25:55.670
Hello, Comrade Fang Zhimin.

469
25:56.080 --> 25:57.810
Corps Commander Xun Huaizhou.

470
25:57.920 --> 25:59.030
Comrade Fang Zhimin.

471
25:59.030 --> 25:59.830
Hello.

472
26:00.110 --> 26:01.350
Chief of Staff Su Yu.

473
26:02.210 --> 26:03.360
Hello.

474
26:03.850 --> 26:05.570
Director of the Political Department, Liu Ying.

475
26:05.570 --> 26:07.660
[Liu Ying, Director of Political Department of the 7th Red Army Corps]

476
26:06.160 --> 26:07.380
Hello, Comrade Fang Zhimin.

477
26:07.380 --> 26:08.420
Hello.

478
26:09.600 --> 26:12.810
[Liu Chouxi, Commander of the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Military District and Commander of the 10th Red Army]

479
26:09.960 --> 26:11.520
This is the Commander of our 10th Red Army,

480
26:11.520 --> 26:12.650
Comrade Liu Chouxi.

481
26:13.530 --> 26:15.730
Thank you for your hard work, comrades.

482
26:16.130 --> 26:16.980
Please.

483
26:17.650 --> 26:18.340
Please.

484
26:19.970 --> 26:21.090
Comrade Fang Zhimin.

485
26:21.090 --> 26:23.170
I've heard so much about you.

486
26:23.480 --> 26:25.780
When I was in the Central Soviet Area, I heard

487
26:25.780 --> 26:28.500
that you established a revolutionary base very early on.

488
26:28.500 --> 26:31.650
Your Soviet area model is known as the Fang Zhimin model.

489
26:32.070 --> 26:34.120
That's Comrade Mao Zedong overpraising me.

490
26:34.120 --> 26:35.460
I just, like Comrade Mao Zedong

491
26:35.460 --> 26:36.660
and Comrade Peng Pai,

492
26:36.890 --> 26:38.380
realized the importance of the peasant movement

493
26:38.380 --> 26:39.380
a bit earlier.

494
26:40.590 --> 26:41.120
This way.

495
26:41.310 --> 26:41.830
Okay.

496
26:43.440 --> 26:44.440
This way, please.

497
26:45.120 --> 26:47.840
On November 4, 1934,

498
26:47.860 --> 26:50.790
according to the orders of the CPC Central Committee and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

499
26:50.790 --> 26:53.120
the 7th Red Army Corps and the 10th Red Army

500
26:53.140 --> 26:55.490
were merged into the 10th Red Army Corps.

501
26:56.160 --> 26:59.640
The 7th Red Army Corps was reorganized into the 19th Division.

502
27:00.240 --> 27:03.440
The 10th Red Army was reorganized into the 20th Division.

503
27:04.110 --> 27:07.010
Liu Chouxi, former Commander of the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Military Region,

504
27:07.010 --> 27:10.740
was appointed Corps Commander and Commander of the 20th Division.

505
27:11.090 --> 27:13.590
Yue Shaohua was appointed Corps Political Commissar

506
27:13.590 --> 27:16.190
and Political Commissar of the 20th Division.

507
27:16.200 --> 27:19.530
Xun Huaizhou was appointed Commander of the 19th Division.

508
27:19.730 --> 27:22.950
Liu Ying was appointed Director of the Political Department.

509
27:22.950 --> 27:27.830
Su Yu was transferred to be Chief of Staff of the Fujian-Zhejiang-Jiangxi Military Region.

510
27:27.830 --> 27:29.470
On November 18,

511
27:29.920 --> 27:32.480
the Military and Political Committee of the 10th Red Army Corps

512
27:32.480 --> 27:35.080
was established with Fang Zhimin as Chairman.

513
27:38.070 --> 27:39.230
According to intelligence,

514
27:39.230 --> 27:41.090
since leaving Jiangxi, the Zhu-Mao Communist forces

515
27:39.680 --> 27:43.810
[Nanchang Headquarters, Jiangxi]

516
27:41.270 --> 27:42.440
has been following the route taken a few months ago

517
27:42.440 --> 27:43.880
by Xiao Ke's troops.

518
27:43.900 --> 27:45.810
They are currently marching from the border of southern Hunan and northern Guangdong

519
27:45.810 --> 27:48.040
towards Lechang and Yizhang.

520
27:49.000 --> 27:50.600
The defense line between Rucheng and Chengkou

521
27:50.600 --> 27:52.000
is practically useless.

522
27:52.070 --> 27:54.030
What are He Jian and Chen Jitang doing?

523
27:54.030 --> 27:55.420
He Jian's main force has not yet assembled,

524
27:55.420 --> 27:56.440
and his troops are limited.

525
27:56.440 --> 27:57.560
The problem is the Guangdong Army.

526
27:57.560 --> 27:59.940
Whenever they encounter the Communist army, they retreat.

527
27:59.940 --> 28:02.480
They always hide behind the Communist army and make empty threats.

528
28:02.480 --> 28:04.440
They block the enemy so clumsily, they might as well announce their arrival,

529
28:04.440 --> 28:06.270
then chase them as if seeing them off.

530
28:06.270 --> 28:08.830
Being so selfish and shirking responsibility,

531
28:07.400 --> 28:08.470
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office]

532
28:08.470 --> 28:09.550
[of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

533
28:08.920 --> 28:09.880
where do they place the Party?

534
28:09.880 --> 28:11.990
They only care about their territory and personal interests.

535
28:11.990 --> 28:14.120
They don't care about the Party at all.

536
28:14.750 --> 28:16.840
Generalissimo, the Zhu-Mao Communist forces are heading west.

537
28:15.360 --> 28:17.190
[Chiang Kai-shek, Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

538
28:17.020 --> 28:19.480
If they join forces with Xiao's and He's troops,

539
28:19.480 --> 28:20.680
it will be a disaster.

540
28:22.750 --> 28:24.670
Send a telegram to He Jian and Chen Jitang,

541
28:24.670 --> 28:27.250
telling them to build a third blockade line around Chen County

542
28:27.250 --> 28:27.940
and Yizhang

543
28:28.500 --> 28:30.110
along the Guangdong-Hankou Railway.

544
28:29.990 --> 28:31.060
[He Guoguang, Director of the 1st Department, Nanchang Headquarters]

545
28:30.200 --> 28:31.200
As for Xue Yue,

546
28:31.250 --> 28:33.280
he should have rested enough in Jiangxi and Fujian.

547
28:33.280 --> 28:34.190
Tell Xue Yue

548
28:34.450 --> 28:36.620
to march day and night to Hunan!

549
28:36.890 --> 28:38.090
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

550
28:40.360 --> 28:44.500
[Guangzhou, Guangdong; Chen Jitang's Residence]

551
28:54.390 --> 28:56.460
[Chen Jitang, Commander-in-Chief of the KMT troops' Southern Route Army and Commander-in-Chief of the Guangdong Army]

552
29:01.450 --> 29:03.310
[Yang Youmin, Major General and Advisor at Guangdong Army Headquarters]

553
29:02.110 --> 29:03.550
Are there any unusual movements from the Communist army?

554
29:03.470 --> 29:07.420
[Yu Hanmou, Commander of the 1st Army of the Guangdong Army]

555
29:04.580 --> 29:05.420
For now,

556
29:06.000 --> 29:06.680
they are basically following

557
29:06.680 --> 29:08.070
what we agreed on before.

558
29:08.070 --> 29:09.690
They are marching only along the Hunan-Guangdong border,

559
29:09.690 --> 29:11.860
looking like the whole army is entering Hunan.

560
29:11.860 --> 29:12.860
Once they leave,

561
29:12.890 --> 29:14.530
Xue Yue will have to enter Hunan,

562
29:14.530 --> 29:16.680
and we will have dodged this bullet.

563
29:16.930 --> 29:18.720
But we are in a dilemma right now.

564
29:18.720 --> 29:20.270
If we continue with the current strategy,

565
29:20.270 --> 29:21.720
how do we explain it to Nanchang?

566
29:21.720 --> 29:23.350
But if we follow Nanchang's telegraphic order

567
29:23.350 --> 29:24.720
to set up defenses along the Guangdong-Hankou line,

568
29:24.720 --> 29:26.310
and really follow the Generalissimo's request

569
29:26.310 --> 29:28.370
to work fast, practically, and hard,

570
29:28.510 --> 29:30.990
then the Communist army will definitely not be able to continue west,

571
29:30.990 --> 29:33.390
and will inevitably go south to Guangdong.

572
29:44.610 --> 29:46.160
It's the word "evade".

573
29:47.940 --> 29:48.830
Evade?

574
29:49.010 --> 29:50.900
Master, what does it mean?

575
29:51.680 --> 29:53.160
In the current situation,

576
29:53.320 --> 29:54.990
with scoundrels in power,

577
29:55.380 --> 29:59.860
a gentleman should avoid provoking them and protect himself,

578
29:59.990 --> 30:02.830
waiting for the opportunity to save the world.

579
30:08.330 --> 30:11.160
Master, your words are enlightening.

580
30:26.290 --> 30:28.350
We must avoid provoking the Red Army,

581
30:28.430 --> 30:30.760
and be even more careful not to provoke the Central Army.

582
30:30.760 --> 30:33.160
Woqi (Yu Hanmou), block first and then suppress.

583
30:33.160 --> 30:34.690
Deploy the main force in depth,

584
30:34.690 --> 30:37.110
compress the Red Army further towards southern Hunan,

585
30:37.110 --> 30:39.370
and ensure they cannot enter Guangdong.

586
30:40.660 --> 30:42.260
We will wait for the opportunity to act.

587
30:42.260 --> 30:43.460
-Yes, sir. -Yes, sir.

588
31:00.290 --> 31:04.260
[Hengyang, Hunan]

589
31:00.830 --> 31:02.070
This Chen Jitang

590
31:02.350 --> 31:04.200
is clearly letting them go on purpose.

591
31:04.200 --> 31:05.800
He has no credibility at all.

592
31:07.130 --> 31:08.160
[He Jian, Commander-in-Chief of the KMT troops' Western Route Army]

593
31:08.000 --> 31:10.480
He's not as good as my Zhongyong.

594
31:08.160 --> 31:09.190
[and Chairman of the Hunan Provincial Government]

595
31:11.810 --> 31:13.850
Today, the heavy burden

596
31:13.870 --> 31:16.310
is all on Hunan.

597
31:15.920 --> 31:18.920
[Liu Jianxu, Commander of the 1st Column of the KMT troops' Western Route Army]

598
31:19.440 --> 31:20.680
Come, Zhongyong.

599
31:20.720 --> 31:21.890
In that case,

600
31:22.170 --> 31:24.170
why don't we follow suit?

601
31:24.470 --> 31:27.800
Why fight to the death with the Communist army?

602
31:28.000 --> 31:28.720
Huixian,

603
31:29.030 --> 31:31.440
are you making fun of me?

604
31:32.300 --> 31:35.410
Chen Jitang has long been secretly colluding with the Communist army.

605
31:35.410 --> 31:37.310
Can I do that?

606
31:38.620 --> 31:39.460
Back then,

607
31:40.370 --> 31:42.930
I killed so many Communists in Changsha,

608
31:43.270 --> 31:46.000
that the Xiang River ran red with blood.

609
31:46.400 --> 31:49.680
And Mao Zedong's wife, Yang Kaihui,

610
31:49.740 --> 31:51.450
was killed by my order.

611
31:52.260 --> 31:53.970
I also ordered the destruction of 3 generations

612
31:53.970 --> 31:59.210
of Mao Zedong's and Peng Dehuai's ancestral graves.

613
31:59.850 --> 32:02.720
The Communist Party and I have a deep hatred.

614
32:03.330 --> 32:04.810
What's more,

615
32:05.700 --> 32:07.570
Chen Jitang and the Guangxi clique's

616
32:07.570 --> 32:09.200
Li Zongren and Bai Chongxi

617
32:09.200 --> 32:10.800
have made Guangdong and Guangxi interdependent

618
32:10.800 --> 32:12.530
and coming to each other's aid.

619
32:13.620 --> 32:16.990
Back then, to support Generalissimo Chiang,

620
32:17.270 --> 32:19.000
I offended everyone.

621
32:20.040 --> 32:22.800
Now, my very survival and standing

622
32:23.770 --> 32:26.500
depend on actively suppressing the Communists.

623
32:28.510 --> 32:29.830
In that case,

624
32:29.850 --> 32:33.160
we can only follow orders?

625
32:33.940 --> 32:35.990
Easier said than done.

626
32:36.020 --> 32:37.260
Just one He Long

627
32:37.470 --> 32:39.470
has already made me exhausted.

628
32:41.360 --> 32:41.990
I think

629
32:42.290 --> 32:45.050
the Generalissimo's New Life Movement

630
32:45.090 --> 32:48.140
is about propriety, justice, honesty, and a sense of shame.

631
32:48.140 --> 32:51.540
As for me, I value the eight virtues,

632
32:52.020 --> 32:53.740
which means the same thing.

633
32:53.930 --> 32:56.650
I have to keep my position first.

634
32:57.020 --> 33:00.210
If I lose my territory, what's the point of virtues?

635
33:01.260 --> 33:05.370
Zhongyong, my little darling, am I right?

636
33:10.030 --> 33:12.730
♪ Rise and shine in the morning ♪

637
33:12.750 --> 33:23.160
♪ Fan your pretty flower fan and take the stage ♪

638
33:24.170 --> 33:27.810
♪ A fresh flower blooms up on the beam ♪

639
33:27.070 --> 33:29.330
Vice Chairman Zhou, an urgent telegram.

640
33:37.320 --> 33:38.540
An urgent telegram from Peng (Peng Dehuai) and Yang (Yang Shangkun)!

641
33:38.540 --> 33:40.670
An urgent telegram from Peng and Yang.

642
33:45.730 --> 33:46.730
The telegram says

643
33:47.240 --> 33:48.720
the Red Army has entered southern Hunan.

644
33:48.720 --> 33:50.440
He Jian is putting up a desperate struggle

645
33:50.440 --> 33:51.920
and will definitely actively cooperate with the Central Army

646
33:51.920 --> 33:53.050
to fight against us.

647
33:53.060 --> 33:55.790
They suggest we quickly and firmly break through

648
33:55.810 --> 33:58.990
the blockade line between Yizhang, Lechang, and Chen County.

649
33:58.990 --> 33:59.860
Map.

650
34:05.370 --> 34:07.780
Comrade Li De, what do you think?

651
34:07.870 --> 34:10.210
If we can quickly break through the enemy's blockade line,

652
34:10.210 --> 34:12.400
I think this plan is feasible.

653
34:13.360 --> 34:15.360
If we can quickly break through the enemy's blockade line,

654
34:15.360 --> 34:16.489
I think this plan is feasible.

655
34:16.489 --> 34:17.110
But right now,

656
34:17.110 --> 34:19.230
the Central Column is moving too slowly.

657
34:19.230 --> 34:20.280
The front and rear are separated

658
34:20.280 --> 34:21.449
by a full 30 kilometers.

659
34:21.449 --> 34:23.850
We simply can't keep up with the field army.

660
34:23.949 --> 34:26.010
Our Central Column must coordinate.

661
34:26.560 --> 34:28.159
We have to speed up our march.

662
34:28.820 --> 34:30.679
Peng and Yang said in the telegram

663
34:31.030 --> 34:34.010
that the Guangdong Army's defense in the Jiufeng Mountain area is weak.

664
34:34.010 --> 34:36.510
We should order the 1st Red Army Corps on the left wing

665
34:36.510 --> 34:37.920
to occupy the commanding heights of Jiufeng Mountain

666
34:37.920 --> 34:39.960
to prevent the enemy from occupying Lechang before us

667
34:39.960 --> 34:42.570
and cutting off our path.

668
34:43.850 --> 34:44.780
Comrade Li De.

669
34:50.300 --> 34:51.179
I agree.

670
34:51.719 --> 34:52.350
I agree.

671
34:52.679 --> 34:53.210
Let's go.

672
34:53.420 --> 34:54.020
Let's go.

673
34:57.010 --> 35:00.910
[Makeng Market, Lechang, Guangdong]

674
34:58.490 --> 35:00.420
There is no enemy presence in Lechang right now.

675
35:00.420 --> 35:01.230
The troops can completely

676
35:01.230 --> 35:02.980
charge directly through the area north of Lechang.

677
35:02.980 --> 35:05.890
There's no need to take a detour to occupy Jiufeng Mountain.

678
35:05.890 --> 35:07.490
The Military Commission ordered us to occupy Jiufeng Mountain

679
35:07.490 --> 35:10.900
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps; Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

680
35:07.760 --> 35:09.770
with overall considerations in mind.

681
35:09.770 --> 35:11.400
Even if we could charge all the way through Lechang,

682
35:11.040 --> 35:12.700
[Geng Biao, Commander of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

683
35:11.960 --> 35:13.120
with the speed of the Military Commission Column,

684
35:12.700 --> 35:14.070
[Zuo Quan, Chief of Staff of the 1st Red Army Corps]

685
35:13.160 --> 35:14.790
they absolutely wouldn't make it.

686
35:14.790 --> 35:17.380
Yesterday, the entire column only advanced 4 kilometers.

687
35:14.810 --> 35:16.190
[Chen Guang, Commander of the 2nd Division of the 1st Red Army Corps]

688
35:18.250 --> 35:19.170
Too slow.

689
35:19.630 --> 35:21.800
Then the Military Commission Column should speed up a bit

690
35:21.800 --> 35:23.030
in case anything goes wrong.

691
35:23.030 --> 35:25.380
Are you going to give suggestions to the Military Commission,

692
35:25.380 --> 35:26.220
or am I?

693
35:26.510 --> 35:27.150
Report!

694
35:28.150 --> 35:28.630
Speak.

695
35:28.650 --> 35:30.250
We followed the enemy's telephone line,

696
35:30.250 --> 35:31.300
and in the ruined temple ahead,

697
35:31.300 --> 35:32.530
we found a telephone.

698
35:34.240 --> 35:34.680
Guard.

699
35:34.700 --> 35:35.180
Here.

700
35:46.430 --> 35:47.490
It's right inside.

701
35:55.330 --> 35:56.250
Hello?

702
35:56.430 --> 35:57.370
What unit is this?

703
35:57.370 --> 35:59.080
I'm with the Laitian Militia, darn it!

704
35:59.080 --> 35:59.770
Who is this?

705
35:59.860 --> 36:00.420
Bastard!

706
36:00.450 --> 36:02.530
I'm with the Central Army's 36th Army.

707
36:02.530 --> 36:04.260
Put your commander on the line.

708
36:04.380 --> 36:05.700
Oh, it's you, sir.

709
36:06.190 --> 36:07.120
Reporting, sir.

710
36:07.290 --> 36:09.350
I am the commander of the Laitian Militia.

711
36:09.350 --> 36:10.420
My surname is Chen.

712
36:10.640 --> 36:12.230
I don't care what your surname is.

713
36:12.230 --> 36:13.110
I'm asking you,

714
36:13.940 --> 36:15.750
where is the Communist army now?

715
36:16.460 --> 36:17.390
Reporting, sir.

716
36:17.440 --> 36:18.840
As for where the Communist army is,

717
36:18.840 --> 36:19.990
I really don't know.

718
36:20.250 --> 36:21.510
What do we feed you for?

719
36:22.170 --> 36:23.260
I'm asking you one more time.

720
36:23.260 --> 36:24.860
Where is the Guangdong Army?

721
36:25.050 --> 36:25.970
As far as I know,

722
36:26.120 --> 36:27.550
the 3 regiments under Commander Deng of the Guangdong Army's

723
36:27.550 --> 36:28.940
4th Independent Division

724
36:28.940 --> 36:30.400
have already taken up positions in Lechang.

725
36:30.400 --> 36:33.270
There is another regiment marching towards Jiufeng Mountain.

726
36:33.270 --> 36:34.030
Commander.

727
36:35.440 --> 36:35.860
Geng Biao.

728
36:35.860 --> 36:36.430
Here.

729
36:36.460 --> 36:37.670
Your 4th Regiment runs fast.

730
36:37.670 --> 36:39.570
Take Jiufeng Mountain at all costs.

731
36:39.570 --> 36:40.290
Set off immediately.

732
36:40.290 --> 36:40.970
Yes, sir.

733
36:51.640 --> 36:52.600
Comrades!

734
36:53.010 --> 36:55.660
We brave the rain, and so does the enemy.

735
36:55.990 --> 36:57.680
The time to test us has come!

736
36:56.260 --> 36:58.970
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment, 2nd Division, 1st Red Army Corps]

737
36:57.970 --> 37:00.620
Taking Jiufeng Mountain means victory!

738
37:16.230 --> 37:17.110
Ma'am.

739
37:17.760 --> 37:18.590
Ma'am.

740
37:18.590 --> 37:19.510
What's wrong?

741
37:19.720 --> 37:21.650
I can't go on anymore. I can't walk.

742
37:22.160 --> 37:23.760
Walking non-stop every day,

743
37:23.860 --> 37:26.190
where are we going?

744
37:27.230 --> 37:28.670
Why did you stop?

745
37:28.700 --> 37:30.380
[Wang Jiaxiang, Vice-Chairman of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission;]

746
37:28.840 --> 37:29.420
I'm exhausted.

747
37:29.420 --> 37:32.460
Jiaxiang, cover yourself with the tarpaulin.

748
37:30.380 --> 37:32.070
[Director of the General Political Department of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army]

749
37:32.640 --> 37:34.170
Don't let the wound get wet.

750
37:35.150 --> 37:35.920
Comrade Zedong,

751
37:35.920 --> 37:37.520
stop worrying about others.

752
37:37.550 --> 37:39.080
You are a patient yourself.

753
37:39.430 --> 37:40.230
What's wrong?

754
37:40.620 --> 37:42.820
We've been following you day and night.

755
37:42.820 --> 37:44.340
When will this ever end?

756
37:45.380 --> 37:46.600
You wander around all day,

757
37:46.600 --> 37:47.480
not knowing where to go.

758
37:47.480 --> 37:48.400
We can't go on any farther.

759
37:48.400 --> 37:48.780
Right.

760
37:48.780 --> 37:50.380
I really can't walk anymore.

761
37:53.900 --> 37:54.600
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), CPC Central Committee Standing Committee Member]

762
37:54.600 --> 37:55.310
[and Chairman of the People's Committee of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

763
37:56.730 --> 37:58.590
Come on, let me bandage you first.

764
37:58.970 --> 38:00.890
It's easy to get infected in the rain.

765
38:00.890 --> 38:01.690
Bear the pain.

766
38:06.310 --> 38:08.970
Fellow villagers, I know you are all very tired.

767
38:09.480 --> 38:10.480
But look,

768
38:10.590 --> 38:11.780
we are in the wilderness,

769
38:11.780 --> 38:13.240
and it's raining heavily.

770
38:13.420 --> 38:15.150
Can you hold on a little longer?

771
38:15.540 --> 38:17.230
Once we reach the next camp,

772
38:17.500 --> 38:18.870
you can collect your wages

773
38:18.870 --> 38:20.930
and fare home, then decide what to do.

774
38:21.550 --> 38:22.030
Come on.

775
38:22.550 --> 38:23.010
Come on.

776
38:23.070 --> 38:23.960
Come on, slowly.

777
38:23.960 --> 38:24.490
Alright.

778
38:24.950 --> 38:27.280
Then we'll take you to the next stop first.

779
38:28.220 --> 38:29.740
Do you have a leader?

780
38:29.640 --> 38:32.280
[Liu Ying, Director of the Political Department of the 3rd Echelon, 2nd Column of the Military Commission]

781
38:29.950 --> 38:31.950
You wander around like this all day.

782
38:32.410 --> 38:34.610
We have families waiting for us at home.

783
38:34.710 --> 38:35.800
If I had known, I wouldn't have tried to earn

784
38:35.800 --> 38:37.000
your money.

785
38:37.560 --> 38:38.090
Let's go.

786
38:38.770 --> 38:39.560
Let's go.

787
38:48.890 --> 38:49.890
Comrade Liu Ying.

788
38:50.590 --> 38:52.050
Come on, Comrade Liu Ying.

789
38:57.470 --> 38:58.430
Chairman Mao.

790
38:58.800 --> 38:59.640
Young lady.

791
39:00.080 --> 39:02.330
You did a good job in ideological work.

792
39:02.780 --> 39:06.570
You are very competent as the director of the political department of the echelon.

793
39:06.570 --> 39:08.260
I didn't do well at all.

794
39:08.720 --> 39:10.120
I'm not competent at all.

795
39:10.150 --> 39:12.500
I didn't solve their problems at all.

796
39:21.740 --> 39:22.780
Comrade Liu Ying.

797
39:23.600 --> 39:26.720
These are a few scripts I've written for living newspaper plays.

798
39:26.720 --> 39:28.150
When you do ideological work,

799
39:28.150 --> 39:29.950
they will definitely be useful.

800
39:32.720 --> 39:33.470
Take them.

801
39:38.550 --> 39:39.550
Go find Li Bozhao.

802
39:39.710 --> 39:40.710
Tell her I said so,

803
39:40.820 --> 39:42.880
and ask her to help you rehearse them.

804
39:43.520 --> 39:45.580
But with the locals feeling this way,

805
39:46.450 --> 39:48.850
what good will these living newspaper plays do?

806
39:48.850 --> 39:51.770
Comrade Liu Ying, they will work.

807
39:52.050 --> 39:54.740
You must believe that the problem can be solved.

808
39:54.880 --> 39:56.000
You need to tell them

809
39:56.000 --> 39:57.370
why we are fighting

810
39:57.920 --> 39:59.450
and who we are fighting for.

811
39:59.920 --> 40:01.360
Don't be afraid of problems.

812
40:01.360 --> 40:02.650
If we all think of a way together,

813
40:02.650 --> 40:03.810
it will be solved.

814
40:04.080 --> 40:05.340
You have to believe it.

815
40:05.340 --> 40:07.600
Isn't Comrade Luofu trying to find a way?

816
40:07.980 --> 40:10.040
He already knows your difficulties.

817
40:10.260 --> 40:12.900
He is trying his best to solve your problems.

818
40:14.590 --> 40:15.670
Comrade Luofu.

819
40:15.890 --> 40:17.340
You are very thoughtful.

820
40:17.520 --> 40:19.050
W-When did you write these?

821
40:20.210 --> 40:22.040
Right, when did you write them?

822
40:22.370 --> 40:23.730
Very thoughtful.

823
40:24.690 --> 40:25.920
You two, honestly!

824
40:26.290 --> 40:27.400
It's a very normal thing.

825
40:27.400 --> 40:28.570
After what you two said,

826
40:28.570 --> 40:30.300
it makes things very delicate.

827
40:30.460 --> 40:31.520
Not just delicate.

828
40:31.660 --> 40:32.700
Comrade Zedong.

829
40:32.730 --> 40:34.900
Her heart is already fluttering.

830
40:35.680 --> 40:36.150
This...

831
40:38.000 --> 40:40.520
Chairman Mao, where are we going?

832
40:40.700 --> 40:43.120
The folks asked me where the destination is.

833
40:43.120 --> 40:44.080
I don't know.

834
40:49.100 --> 40:50.230
I don't know either.

835
40:51.570 --> 40:53.300
But we will definitely find it.

836
40:54.310 --> 40:56.570
You have to believe it, Comrade Liu Ying.

837
40:57.700 --> 40:58.430
Definitely.

838
41:09.480 --> 41:11.850
Comrade Luofu, thank you.

839
41:13.130 --> 41:14.660
Thank you for your scripts.

840
41:30.370 --> 41:32.340
No one knows where the army is headed—

841
41:32.340 --> 41:33.830
not the soldiers,

842
41:33.860 --> 41:35.230
not Liu Ying,

843
41:35.620 --> 41:38.570
not even the Red Army's senior commanders.

844
41:39.390 --> 41:41.190
However, at this very moment,

845
41:41.210 --> 41:42.610
thousands of miles away,

846
41:43.080 --> 41:45.560
in Liyuanbao, Nanliang, Qingyang, Gansu,

847
41:45.960 --> 41:48.440
a ceremony is being held to establish

848
41:48.460 --> 41:51.460
the Soviet Government of the Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region.

849
41:48.820 --> 41:52.750
[Liyuanbao, Nanliang, Qingyang, Gansu]

850
41:55.760 --> 42:01.030
Great!

851
41:58.220 --> 41:59.070
[Liu Zhidan, Chairman of the Revolutionary Military Commission of the Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region]

852
41:59.070 --> 42:00.780
[Xi Zhongxun, Chairman of the Soviet Government of the Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region]

853
42:02.070 --> 42:04.480
Great! Great! Great!

854
42:06.880 --> 42:08.920
Boy Chairman! Boy Chairman!

855
42:09.320 --> 42:11.720
I think you have to say a few words

856
42:11.750 --> 42:13.350
to our folks today.

857
42:13.770 --> 42:14.630
Say a few words.

858
42:17.290 --> 42:18.480
What's the fuss?

859
42:19.200 --> 42:20.510
He is the Chairman.

860
42:20.640 --> 42:22.170
Why call him a boy Chairman?

861
42:22.200 --> 42:24.110
You woman, what do you know?

862
42:24.330 --> 42:25.080
I mean,

863
42:25.340 --> 42:29.700
our Chairman Xi is young and promising,

864
42:29.730 --> 42:30.860
isn't he, everyone?

865
42:30.920 --> 42:31.630
Yes!

866
42:33.960 --> 42:35.020
Comrade Zhongxun.

867
42:35.340 --> 42:36.870
Say a few words to everyone.

868
42:37.570 --> 42:38.080
Say a few words.

869
42:38.080 --> 42:38.480
Great!

870
42:39.300 --> 42:39.970
Great!

871
42:49.940 --> 42:51.940
Comrades, folks,

872
42:52.440 --> 42:55.690
today, our Shaanxi-Gansu Border Region Soviet Government

873
42:55.690 --> 42:57.290
is officially established!

874
42:59.510 --> 43:04.360
Great! Great! Great!
